CAT = "dronScope"; SEG = "SCO"
Q = [
("Under Part 101, which of these is a remotely piloted aircraft?",
 "A radio controlled model plane", ["A control line model plane", "A free flight model glider", "A kite held on a long line"],
 "Part 101 defines a remotely piloted aircraft as an unmanned aircraft piloted from a remote station, and says it includes a radio controlled model aircraft. Control line and free flight model aircraft are defined separately."),
("What is the heaviest gross mass of remotely piloted aircraft that may be flown under Part 101?",
 "25 kg", ["15 kg", "20 kg", "30 kg"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 2.15 says a remotely piloted aircraft must not be flown with a gross mass of more than 25 kg. Anything heavier needs a Part 102 operator certificate."),
("A drone weighs 18 kg. What does it need before it can fly under Part 101?",
 "An approved person's authority", ["A Part 47 aircraft registration", "A NOTAM for every flight", "A Part 61 private pilot licence"],
 "Between 15 kg and 25 kg the aircraft and any change to it must be built under the authority of, or inspected and approved by, an approved person or organisation, and flown under that authority (CATI 101-1 clause 2.15)."),
("Does a drone flown under Part 101 need to be registered under Part 47?",
 "No, Part 47 does not apply", ["Yes, before its first flight", "Only if flown for business", "Only if over 250 g"],
 "Rule 101.5 says the registration requirements of Part 47 do not apply to unmanned aircraft, kites, rockets, parasails and gyrogliders."),
("Who makes a civil aviation transport instrument under Part 101?",
 "The Director", ["The Minister of Transport", "Airways New Zealand", "The local council"],
 "Rule 101.17 says a transport instrument for Part 101 may be made by the Director under section 431 of the Civil Aviation Act 2023."),
("What is the legal status of CATI 101-1?",
 "Secondary legislation", ["Voluntary guidance", "A code of practice only", "An Airways policy"],
 "Rule 101.17 says a transport instrument is secondary legislation. AC101-1 adds that breaching CATI 101-1 is a breach of the matching Part 101 rule."),
("Which document is an acceptable means of compliance, rather than a rule, for flying a drone under Part 101?",
 "Advisory Circular AC101-1", ["Transport instrument CATI 101-1", "Civil Aviation Rule 101.209", "The Civil Aviation Act 2023"],
 "Advisory circulars set out practices the Director accepts as a way to comply. Part 101 and CATI 101-1 are law, and the transport instrument holds most of the Subpart E details."),
("A farmer wants to spot stock with a 2 kg drone for her business. Can she fly under Part 101?",
 "Yes, Part 101 covers it", ["No, business needs Part 102", "Only after Part 47 registration", "Only with a Part 61 licence"],
 "AC101-1 says Part 101 applies to recreational and commercial users, so commercial work can be done without certification while the operator keeps to Part 101 and CATI 101-1."),
("An operation cannot meet the Part 101 rules. What must the operator hold to fly it?",
 "A Part 102 certificate", ["A Part 47 registration", "An Airshare account", "A model club membership card"],
 "Rule 102.7 says a person must not fly an unmanned aircraft other than in accordance with Part 101 unless they hold an unmanned aircraft operator certificate under Part 102."),
("A Part 102 certificate holder flies a task that Part 101 also allows. Under which authority is it flown?",
 "The Part 102 certificate", ["Part 101 alone", "Both, at the pilot's choice", "Neither, it needs an exemption"],
 "Rule 102.17(c) says a certificate holder exercising a privilege that applies under both Part 101 and Part 102 is deemed to exercise it under the Part 102 certificate."),
("What is the longest term the Director may give a Part 102 operator certificate?",
 "5 years", ["1 year", "2 years", "10 years"],
 "Rule 102.19 says the expiry date the Director sets may not be later than 5 years after the certificate was granted."),
("A Part 102 certificate holder must comply with Part 101 to what extent?",
 "Where it fits its operations", ["Not at all, Part 101 is replaced", "Only for flights over 25 kg", "Only for flights at night"],
 "Rule 102.21 requires the holder to comply with Part 101 to the extent it is consistent with the operations specified in the operations specification, plus the Director's conditions and the exposition."),
("Which of these is a function an approved person or organisation can be approved for under rule 101.202?",
 "Issuing pilot qualifications", ["Granting Part 102 certificates", "Registering drones under Part 47", "Approving airspace changes"],
 "Rule 101.202 lists functions such as issuing a pilot qualification, appointing instructors, authorising NOTAM notifications and approving aircraft between 15 kg and 25 kg. Part 102 certificates are granted by the Director."),
("Under Part 101, what is a control line model aircraft?",
 "One flown in circles on wires", ["One flown by radio", "One with no control after launch", "One tethered like a kite"],
 "Part 101 defines a control line model aircraft as one controlled through a single or multiple wire system held by the person flying it, restricted to circular flight about a central point."),
("How long may the wire system of a control line model aircraft be?",
 "No longer than 30 m", ["No longer than 15 m", "No longer than 50 m", "No longer than 100 m"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 2.1 says a person must not fly a control line model aircraft with a single or multiple wire system longer than 30 m."),
("Under Part 101, what makes a model aircraft a free flight model aircraft?",
 "Its path can't be steered", ["It flies on a control line", "It weighs less than 250 g", "It flies only indoors"],
 "A free flight model aircraft has a flight path that, once launched, is uncontrollable, and a wing loading of no more than 62 g per square decimetre (Part 101 definitions)."),
("For a term defined in both Part 1 and Part 101, such as aerodrome, which definition applies to a drone pilot?",
 "The Part 101 definition", ["The Part 1 definition", "The AIP's own definition", "The ICAO Annex definition"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 1.5 and AC101-1 both say that when a term is defined in Part 1 and Part 101, the Part 101 definition applies."),
("Under Part 101, which places count as an aerodrome?",
 "Those promulgated in the AIPNZ", ["Any paddock used for landing", "Only airports with a tower", "Only airports with airline flights"],
 "Part 101 defines an aerodrome as one promulgated in the current AIPNZ (Aeronautical Information Publication New Zealand)."),
("Which rule part covers unmanned aircraft operator certification in New Zealand?",
 "Part 102", ["Part 47", "Part 61", "Part 107"],
 "Part 102 sets the certification and operation of unmanned aircraft outside Part 101. Part 47 is aircraft registration and Part 61 is pilot licences."),
("Who is responsible for a drone flight being safe even when every rule has been followed?",
 "The drone's operator", ["The drone's manufacturer", "The Civil Aviation Authority", "Airways New Zealand"],
 "AC101-1 says that even if an operator complies with all the rules, they are still obliged to make sure they do not fly in a hazardous manner, so they must plan for the hazards."),
("What may happen to someone who breaks the civil aviation rules while flying a drone?",
 "They may be prosecuted", ["Nothing, the rules are advice", "Only a written reminder", "Only loss of the drone's warranty"],
 "The CAA's drone brochure warns that breaching New Zealand civil aviation rules while flying an unmanned aircraft can lead to disciplinary action including prosecution."),
("Under rule 101.202, an approved organisation may authorise one type of drone work for heavier aircraft. Which?",
 "Building a 15 to 25 kg RPA", ["Flying an RPA over 25 kg", "Spraying crops from an RPA", "Flying an RPA beyond sight"],
 "Rule 101.202 lets an approved person or organisation authorise the construction, modification, inspection and operation of an RPA greater than 15 kg but not greater than 25 kg. Over 25 kg needs Part 102."),
("Does a drone pilot flying under Part 101 always need a pilot qualification?",
 "No, only for some operations", ["Yes, for every flight", "Yes, if the drone has a camera", "Yes, if flown for business"],
 "AC101-1 says Part 101 operators do not need a pilot qualification unless an unshielded flight takes place within 4 km of an aerodrome boundary. Unshielded night flying needs an approved night course."),
("What does the term RPAS add to remotely piloted aircraft?",
 "The remote station and links", ["The pilot's licence and logbook", "The aircraft's insurance cover", "The flight's NOTAM details"],
 "AC101-1 defines a remotely piloted aircraft system as the aircraft plus its remote pilot station or stations, the command and control links and any other components needed to fly it."),
]
